Subject: [PATCH 01903/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1
 (HEADLINE BUILD; STRENGTHEN) -- BUILD a CROSS-CANDIDATE SET-ENCODER
 AGGREGATOR for the oracle-distinct ARC verifier, fixing the .391 null's three
 causes. .391's build (exp4220) was a per-candidate LOGISTIC REGRESSION
 (scored each candidate in ISOLATION) trained on 14 ACCEPTED / 1782 REJECTED
 rows (base-rate 0.008, off-fold AUROC 0.779). FIX: (1) CROSS-CANDIDATE
 features/architecture -- a permutation-invariant set-encoder over the
 per-task candidate set (Set-Encoder 2404.06912; MSV 2603.03417
 cross-sequence; AggLM 2509.06870 review/reconcile) so each candidate is
 scored CONDITIONED on its competitors (vote basin, cross-candidate agreement,
 competing transformation families); (2) CALIBRATED imbalance-aware loss
 (2509.19681: class-weighted/focal + temperature/isotonic calibration +
 stratified-balanced minibatches) so the 14-positive slice does not wash out;
 (3) GROW the labeled pool toward >=30 held-out wrong-majority tasks (reuse
 scripts/exp_verifier_detector_auroc.py:load_arc_rows over the GAP-4 pools;
 add games if available). Out-of-fold; verifier_is_oracle=false. Report
 off-fold AUROC + aggregator_trained + learned_verifier_path +
 wrong_majority_n + held_out_task_n. Honest no-learnable-signal is COMPLETE
 and still persists for A2.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
